HIGH 3 -- what LOSE_CHARGE on Ar+ actually produces
==============================================================================
  declared Ar+.decrement_charge = ['Ar0']
  declared Ar0.increment_charge = ['Ar+']

  bare Ar+   u1 p3 c+1            perceives as Ar+
    LOSE_CHARGE -> u1 p3 c+0 -> Ar0e
  bonded Ar+ u0 p3 c+1 (1 single) perceives as Ar+
    LOSE_CHARGE -> u0 p3 c+0 1 single -> Ar0s

  inverses (GAIN_CHARGE), to see what would have to close back:
    Ar0      (Ar0  ) GAIN_CHARGE -> u0 p4 c+1 -> <no type>
    Ar0e     (Ar0e ) GAIN_CHARGE -> u2 p3 c+1 -> Ar+
    Ar0s u1  (Ar0s ) GAIN_CHARGE -> u1 p3 c+1 -> Ar+
    Ar0s u0  (Ar0s ) GAIN_CHARGE -> u0 p3 c+1 -> Ar+

